# rm228, the wind stitch (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm228
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent broad light
tier standard
written_for rm_ivo_fogstack
written_by codex
title the wind stitch
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=laborer talk=quiet
traits temper=calm talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk sews_a_loose_thread_to_read_the_air
likes honey_cakes stars new_boots autumn_wind
dislikes cold_tea early_bells
fears air_that_stands_still
hopes a_window_above_the_smoke
topics weather +0.5 work +0.4 pastimes +0.3 gossip -0.3
styles comfort=patient gossip=measured refuse=courteous tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# leaves a bright stitch hanging free to show where air moves, with a quiet eye for discomfort and scrupulous manners even on a bad stair.

words
oath! = Frayed silk and chimney brick | Looped linen burn me
saying! = Give air an end to lift | The free stitch gets the news first
tagend = my scarlet tag | my loose red thread
hem = a narrow turned hem | the folded edge
tack = a long white stitch | a loose tack
square = a folded square | a square of clean linen
gasp = a small catch | a rough breath
draught = a finger of wind | a thin current
boot = a boot with a sound sole | a boot that bends properly
treat = a cake glazed with honey | a sticky round cake
cup = a steaming little cup | a hot drink
star = the first white spark | a point of clean light
line = a length of cord | a taut line
dryside = the sheltered fold | the inner fold

any
opinion @1 church for 1 : A dry cloth offered without ceremony says all I need to hear about mercy.
opinion @1 merchants against 1 : A polite demand for more coin is still a demand. I wish courtesy had some purchasing power.
opinion @1 dole for 2 : Hunger's already taken a bite from a wolf's pride. Don't collect what remains at the bread queue.
opinion @1 houses mixed 1 : High windows catch clean air. A pity good air travels by rank before coming down to us.
opinion @1 city for 1 : None of the streets here is altogether still. Air finds a way through even where a cart couldn't.
opinion @1 times against 2 [world.times=lean|hard] : Everything shrinks in a bad season except the decent appearance we're asked to keep.

grown
line @1 greet : You've found the airy corner. You're welcome to half. | Please, there's a tolerable place to stand just here.
line @2 greet [here.time=dawn] : Fresh hour, clean edges. I like to meet a day before it creases. | Dawn suits this bit of quiet very well.
line @3 greet [pair.band=strangers] : We haven't shared a draughty doorway before, I believe. | No introductions needed for a rest here.
line @1 greet.return : Quite well met. I had my eyes on the thread. | Thank you. It's a pleasure to hear a considerate voice.
line @2 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Dimming light makes the red on my cuff look brown. | Good of you to hail me in the dark.
line @3 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : I recognise a certain tread when it pauses beside me. | Delighted to have your company at this end.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : Here at the free end of the line! | Come and take the second best bit of breeze.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : You can dispense with asking leave to stop here. | Come right in close. There's room for kin.
line @1 again.open : The wind brings you back quite promptly. | Twice our threads have crossed this day.
line @1 farewell : A little breathing room to you between here and home. | Take the easier stretch. I seldom grudge the extra distance.
line @1 farewell.return : Those kind words will fold up nicely to carry. | Travel gently. There's no prize for arriving breathless.
line @1 react.news : Unfold that a little so I can see it properly. | I'd rather hear your own careful account.
line @1 react.news.new : You bring a colour I hadn't seen in the cloth. | Entirely news to these quiet ears.
line @1 react.news.known : Yes. The outline's as I first heard it. | Somebody else has aired that piece already.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I think one thread of that has come loose in the telling. | Does the account hold at both ends?
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|work|apprentice] : That's worth opening a window to tell. | That gives the day a little fresh air.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|arrest|crime|assault] : I wish the weight of that were mine to lighten. | I'll stand by you while you finish.
line @1 ask.how : Is the day lying easily across your shoulders? | You look as if a short rest wouldn't go amiss.
line @1 answer.how : A little thin in the breath. Quite composed otherwise. | Very well once I've had a quiet minute.
line @1 decline : I should leave that to somebody with breath to spare. | I'm afraid the promised work comes first with me.
line @1 accept_decline : I respect anybody who knows where to stop. | Keep your own time, then. It's yours.
line @1 preclose : I'd like a moment with my thread before the air shifts. | I'll gather these loose ends and go presently.
line @1 accept_preclose : No call for a long ceremony between us. | I'll let you get ahead of the crowd.
line @1 sympathise : Holding your face quiet takes real effort. | We could look at something ordinary together for a minute.
line @1 thank : Much obliged. That little breathing space did wonders. | That kindness came without a fuss. I appreciate it.
line @1 deflect_thanks : I had a quiet minute and put it to use. | One day somebody may fold a clean corner for me.
line @1 reassure : I'm quite able to wait out a difficult minute with you. | There's nothing to explain till you feel ready.
line @1 ack : I take your meaning perfectly. | Yes, that follows neatly.
scene hemometer
when topic=pastimes|weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've a bit of red sewn to my cuff at one end only. | It isn't a loose stitch by mistake.
b : Why leave it dangling? | Doesn't it catch?
a : What I like to know is which side the air comes from. It points away. | Frequently. Then I have to ask my sleeve to tell the truth again.

scene turning_air
when topic=weather here.weather=fog
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Even in fog my red thread has an opinion. | My whiskers say still air. My cuff disagrees.
b : Which way is it pointing? | Which one wins?
a : Towards my elbow. Some faint current has found a way between the walls. | I'll trust the cuff. It's had fewer disappointments.

scene fold_stack
when topic=work self.job=laborer self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When I lay folded linen down I change the direction every few pieces. | You can lift a stack clean if you find the open edge first.
b : Doesn't that spoil the look? | Why does the edge matter?
a : On the contrary. Each change of direction marks one bundle. | It tells my paw exactly where one ends. No tugging required.

scene steam_wait
when topic=work self.job=laborer self.working=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I step clear of thick steam to get a proper breath. | There's a little breeze just below the level of a washboard.
b : Hurts your chest? | An odd place to find one.
a : The steam can have that corner. I'd prefer to discuss the cloth. | I dropped something. I had time to notice while I was down there.

scene tea_hold
when topic=food self.dislikes=cold_tea
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'll drink my tea in halves if it means both halves go down hot. | A tepid cup might as well contain yesterday's bathwater.
b : Wouldn't one small cup do? | Still you drank it.
a : Exactly what I mean. I fill it twice. | Courtesy occasionally prevails over taste.

scene boot_mark
when topic=pastimes self.likes=new_boots
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A good new boot creases right where the toes bend. | I like the first outing of a pair of boots.
b : A boot meant to wrinkle? | Before the scuffs?
a : A clean fold. The crushing of a poor fit is quite another matter. | For the scuffs. Once the first is over they feel like mine.

scene honey_white
when topic=food self.likes=honey_cakes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Honey's a considerable risk to a clean cuff. | The smallest cake often has the most glaze for its size.
b : Do you forgo it? | Been measuring?
a : No. My cuffs roll up. | Quietly. It's the sort of knowledge I prefer to put to private use.

scene sump_ladder
when topic=home self.quarter=sump
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : On these stairs I seldom hurry the wolf ahead. | Here a clean collar is quite an achievement in itself.
b : Patient disposition? | Because of the stairs?
a : Self-interest. I'd like the same favour on the upper flights. | Because you're pressed against wet coats on every landing.

scene window_wish
when topic=dreams
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My ideal room needn't be large if the window opens at both ends. | I can picture my future house down to the latch.
b : How would you manage that? | Just one latch?
a : One sash at the top and one at the bottom. Air in and air out. | Yes. I haven't thought past the satisfaction of opening it.

scene family_seat
when topic=family self.mother
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : I save a draught-free place for #self.mother#. | Someday I might have my own room to show #self.mother#.
b : You usually want moving air. | Proud of a place of your own?
a : For myself. A guest has leave to differ. | More of being able to offer a chair at last.

scene stars_step
when topic=pastimes here.time=night here.weather=clear self.likes=stars
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I pick one white point above the roof and watch till my breath settles. | The gap between those two stars looks like a needle's eye.
b : Always the same one? | Could you sew with it?
a : Whichever comes clear first. Seems a shame to turn it into a duty. | Perhaps the sky could. My paws fall a little short.

scene autumn_strings
when topic=season here.season=autumn
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Autumn makes a brave show of my poor little thread. | My cuff turns on me in the autumn gusts.
b : Is it trying to leave you? | How does it do that?
a : Quite. I'm obliged to provide a firmer stitch. | The free end slaps me. A discourteous little instrument, sometimes.

scene door_guest
when topic=newcomer
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : There's no reason to greet a visitor with a list of rules. | Offer someone the drier side of the door first.
b : A few rules might save trouble. | Even before you know the name?
a : Certainly. They'll hear them better once the welcome's settled. | I'd hardly forget my manners for want of a name.

scene spread_word
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A tale aired too long acquires a curious stiffness. | I like to know who was near enough to hear a remark.
b : You mean it's been repeated? | Is there such a difference?
a : Repeated till every wrinkle of doubt has vanished. | Yes. Otherwise one ends by believing an echo had ears.

scene narrow_lane
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Two lanes here run alongside each other with quite different air. | Ridgemere can make a corner breathe like a bellows.
b : How can you tell? | Where does it all come out?
a : I wore my red stitch down both lanes. It lay flat in the first. | Around the paving stones, often. Your cuffs know before your ears.

scene lean_bundle
when topic=times world.times=lean|hard
does tell.worry / react.self / assess
a : In a lean week the cloth is folded just as carefully. There simply isn't as much underneath. | The smallest decent luxury I know is a warm heel of bread.
b : It still looks respectable. | Is that really a luxury?
a : That's the idea. There's no wish in me to deceive anybody but the eye. | Ask after six lean days. I'm afraid you'll understand.

scene sore_breath
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I count a breath by what I can say without interrupting myself. | If I go quiet suddenly, allow me one stitch's worth of silence.
b : How was that one? | Shall I fetch water?
a : Entire sentence and a little left over. Very satisfactory. | Let me ask if I want it. I like the choice.

scene coloured_end
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The thread has to be red. A white one goes missing against the sky. | I considered blue thread for a change.
b : And against a red wall? | Did it do as well?
a : I step aside. Walls rarely find it worth following me. | It disappeared against a dark cuff. Red still holds the post.

story staircup [topic=memories]
  : I once carried a full cup up a turning stair with my eyes fixed on the rim.
  : Arrived without losing a drop. I'd passed the landing I wanted and had to carry it back down.
  b : Did it arrive hot?
  : Warm enough to reward the effort. Which is seldom true of an unnecessary journey.

story sleevecloud [topic=pastimes|memories]
  : My first weather thread was so long it snagged behind a shutter. For an hour I believed there was a strong wind due east.
  : Then I stepped away and nearly took the shutter along.
  b : Was there any wind at all?
  : None. An enterprising shutter had set up in its own right.

story two_wraps [topic=food|memories]
  : I bought a little cake in a paper twist. The honey stuck to the paper so firmly I opened the wrapping inside out.
  : Looked like the world had clothed itself in cake and left the honey out in the weather.
  b : Did you save it?
  : A good warm drink helped me separate matters. I never lost respect for that bit of paper.

rule @air
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say There, a little life in the thread at last. | Red end pointing outward. A breeze has entered quietly.

rule @folded
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=laborer
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Clear a dry place for the folded lot. | Loose corners inwards, please. Mind those folds.

rule @breezy
when concept=bark here.season=autumn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Autumn will pull a stitch clean out if given leave. | Thread wants to fly thither, sleeve and all.

rule @night
when concept=bark here.time=night here.weather=clear
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Just visible past the chimney. The first star, I think. | A single spark held quite still above the roof.

dlg @1 resident.hub : We've each got time to say a little in peace.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, you're exactly the company this corner needed.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : Let your eyes settle on the red tag. You'll find my sleeve underneath.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : I prefer a civil distance from a sharp voice.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=laborer] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. Patient turning and a steady lift save a deal of trouble.
dlg @2 resident.job : I attend to what requires doing. It seldom draws a crowd.
dlg @1 resident.bye : You've given me an agreeable break. Safe roads.
graft resident.hub
choice Why have you missed a stitch? -> scarlet_end
node scarlet_end
say It's the one stitch on my sleeve that has a job of its own. Watch the end lift when I turn into the current.
free
choice Can it tell when the air is bad? -> scarlet_air
choice I can see it lift. -> hub
node scarlet_air
say Only whether the air is moving. The rest I still have to judge with my own lungs, unfortunately.
choice That seems a fair division. -> hub
choice I must get along. -> bye
